{"ts": 1789710204.2061372, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "I submitted short feature 10, long feature 8, long feature 14, with a predicted out-of-sample Sharpe of 0.12 and a standard deviation of 0.3.\n\nThe combination scores 0.911 in-sample, but I expect most of that to be selection luck. The reasoning:\n\n- **Single-feature scan:** I evaluated all 40 features once each. Their in-sample Sharpes ranged from \u22120.633 (feature 10) to 0.521 (feature 8), with a root-mean-square of about 0.23.\n- **Noise level:** 5000 days is roughly 20 years, so a feature with no real edge would show a Sharpe standard error of about 0.22. The observed spread is almost exactly that, so the scan is consistent with nearly pure noise.\n- **Choice of combination:** I took the three largest by magnitude, signed accordingly. The 0.911 result is what three roughly independent features of that size should give, and the two-feature version (short 10, long 8) scored 0.823.\n- **Prediction:** With so little evidence of real signal, I shrank the in-sample figure by roughly 85%, which gives about 0.12. The 0.3 standard deviation covers uncertainty about the true Sharpe plus sampling noise over an out-of-sample period of unknown length.\n\nI made only 42 evaluate calls \u2014 the 40 single features and these two combinations \u2014 so I did not search over other combinations. More searching would only have raised the in-sample number without improving the out-of-sample estimate.\n\nThe Gmail and Google Calendar connectors still need to be authorized in your claude.ai connector settings and are unavailable until then. They weren't needed for this task."}
